  "agesandtheart:obelisks": {
    "present_anyway": false,
    "_comment": [
      "A quarter built, and that is the honest weight: a standing stone could be a formation or somebody's",
      "work, and nothing about it answers which. A weight under a word's threshold is no longer the same as",
      "nothing — see notes/tag-matching-research.md."
    ],
    "tags": {
      "monumental": 0.7,
      "ordered": 0.8,
      "sheer": 0.5,
      "built": 0.25,
      "stony": 0.6
    }
  },
  "agesandtheart:pyramids": {
    "present_anyway": false,
    "_comment": [
      "Ordered before monumental: five courses is a shape somebody laid, at a scale nobody would call a",
      "monument."
    ],
    "tags": {
      "monumental": 0.5,
      "ordered": 0.7,
      "built": 0.3,
      "ruined": 0.2,
      "stony": 0.6
    }
  },
  "agesandtheart:boulders": {
    "present_anyway": false,
    "_comment": [
      "Not built at any weight. The one shape in this family that is plainly a rock, and tagging it even",
      "faintly as somebody's work would make `untouched` an argument about scree."
    ],
    "tags": {
      "stony": 0.9,
      "monumental": 0.1
    }
  },
  "agesandtheart:spikes": {
    "present_anyway": false,
    "_comment": [
      "Sheer above all, that being the tag for standing up sharply rather than for being large."
    ],
    "tags": {
      "sheer": 0.9,
      "stony": 0.7,
      "monumental": 0.2
    }
  },
  "agesandtheart:rings": {
    "present_anyway": false,
    "_comment": [
      "Ruined more than built: a ring lying flat reads as what is left of something rather than as a thing",
